---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Trade Show & Convention Models | Carve Model"
  description="Custom architectural models for trade shows and conventions, planned around portability, booth space, protective packaging and setup across multiple venues."
  canonicalPath="/trade-show-convention-models"
  ogTitle="Trade Show & Convention Models | Carve Model"
  ogDescription="Custom architectural models for trade shows and conventions, planned around portability, booth space, protective packaging and setup across multiple venues."
  active="services"
  imageSlot={true}
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={`{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Service","@id":"https://www.physical-model.com/trade-show-convention-models#service","url":"https://www.physical-model.com/trade-show-convention-models","name":"Trade Show & Convention Models","serviceType":"Architectural models for trade shows and conventions","description":"Custom architectural models for trade shows and conventions, planned around portability, booth space, protective packaging and setup across multiple venues.","provider":{"@id":"https://www.physical-model.com/#organization"},"areaServed":[{"@type":"Country","name":"United States"},{"@type":"Country","name":"Canada"}],"isPartOf":{"@id":"https://www.physical-model.com/#website"},"breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://www.physical-model.com/trade-show-convention-models#breadcrumb"}}`} />
<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={`{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","@id":"https://www.physical-model.com/trade-show-convention-models#breadcrumb","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.physical-model.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Services","item":"https://www.physical-model.com/scale-model-services"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Architectural & Real Estate Models","item":"https://www.physical-model.com/architectural-scale-models"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":4,"name":"Trade Show & Convention Models","item":"https://www.physical-model.com/trade-show-convention-models"}]}`} />
<style>
.breadcrumb{padding-top:1.6rem;}
.breadcrumb a{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.8rem;letter-spacing:0.04em;color:var(--cm-text-subtle);transition:color var(--dur-2);}
.breadcrumb a:hover{color:var(--cm-text-strong);}
.page-hero{padding-top:1.6rem;padding-bottom:clamp(2.5rem,4vw,4rem);border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);}
.page-hero h1{margin-top:1.4rem;}
.page-hero h1 em{font-style:normal;color:var(--cm-text-muted);}
.page-hero p{margin-top:1.4rem;}
.page-hero__inner{display:grid;grid-template-columns:0.85fr 1.15fr;gap:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,3rem);align-items:center;}
@media(max-width:900px){.page-hero__inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.page-hero__visual{order:-1;max-width:440px;}}
.page-hero__visual{position:relative;}
.page-hero__visual image-slot{width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:4/3;border-radius:var(--r-sm);}
.page-hero__visual .corner{position:absolute;width:14px;height:14px;border:1px solid var(--cm-silver);opacity:0.5;z-index:3;}
.page-hero__visual .corner.tl{top:-1px;left:-1px;border-right:0;border-bottom:0;}
.page-hero__visual .corner.br{bottom:-1px;right:-1px;border-left:0;border-top:0;}
.hero__spec{position:absolute;right:-12px;bottom:24px;z-index:4;background:var(--cm-ink-800);border:1px solid var(--cm-border-strong);padding:0.9rem 1.1rem;box-shadow:var(--shadow-lg);}
.hero__spec .tick{display:block;}
.hero__spec strong{font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:var(--w-bold);color:var(--cm-text-strong);font-size:1.15rem;letter-spacing:-0.01em;}
.hero__cta{display:flex;gap:0.9rem;flex-wrap:nowrap;margin-top:1.8rem;}
@media(max-width:560px){.hero__cta{flex-wrap:wrap;}}
.hero__cta .btn--primary,.hero__cta .btn--ghost{background:transparent;color:var(--cm-text-strong);border:1px solid var(--cm-border-strong);}
.hero__cta .btn--primary:hover,.hero__cta .btn--ghost:hover{background:var(--cm-accent);color:var(--cm-accent-contrast);border-color:var(--cm-accent);}
.svc-all-btn{background:transparent;color:var(--cm-text-strong);}
.svc-all-btn:hover{background:var(--cm-accent);color:var(--cm-accent-contrast);border-color:var(--cm-accent);}
.dedi-media{margin-top:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);}
.dedi-media image-slot{width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:21/9;}
.dedi-body{padding-block:clamp(3rem,5vw,5rem);}
.dedi-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:clamp(2rem,4vw,4rem);align-items:start;}
.dedi-grid h2{font-size:clamp(1.6rem,2.8vw,2.4rem);letter-spacing:-0.02em;}
.dedi-list{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:1.4rem 0 0;display:grid;gap:0.8rem;}
.dedi-list li{display:flex;gap:0.7rem;align-items:flex-start;font-size:1rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);}
.dedi-list li svg{flex:none;margin-top:4px;color:var(--cm-silver);}
@media(max-width:820px){.dedi-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}
.svc-section{padding-block:clamp(3rem,5vw,5rem);border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);}
.svc-section h2{font-size:clamp(1.6rem,2.8vw,2.4rem);letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin-top:1rem;}
.svc-section .lead-p{margin-top:1.2rem;max-width:68ch;}
.svc-checklist{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:1.8rem 0 0;display:grid;gap:0.75rem;max-width:68ch;}
.svc-checklist li{display:flex;gap:0.7rem;align-items:flex-start;font-size:1rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);}
.svc-checklist li svg{flex:none;margin-top:4px;color:var(--cm-silver);}
.svc-types{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.6rem);margin-top:2rem;}
.svc-type{padding-top:0;border-top:0;}
.svc-type__media{margin-bottom:0.9rem;}
.svc-type__media image-slot{width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:4/3;border-radius:var(--r-sm);}
.svc-type h3{font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:var(--w-semibold);color:var(--cm-text-strong);letter-spacing:-0.01em;}
.svc-type p{margin-top:0.5rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);font-size:0.9rem;max-width:none;}
@media(max-width:760px){.svc-types{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}
.svc-steps{display:grid;gap:0;margin-top:2rem;max-width:68ch;}
.svc-step{display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.4rem 1fr;gap:1rem;padding-block:1rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);}
.svc-step:last-child{border-bottom:0;}
.svc-step__n{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--cm-text-subtle);padding-top:0.15rem;}
.svc-step p{color:var(--cm-text-muted);font-size:1rem;}
.svc-note{margin-top:1.4rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);max-width:68ch;}
.formats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1px;background:var(--cm-line-faint);border:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);margin-top:1.8rem;}
.fmt{position:relative;background:var(--cm-ink-900);padding:1.4rem 1rem;text-align:center;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--cm-gray-300);letter-spacing:0.03em;transition:background var(--dur-3),color var(--dur-3);}
.fmt:hover{background:var(--cm-ink-850);color:var(--cm-text-strong);}
@media(max-width:760px){.formats{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);}}
@media(max-width:480px){.formats{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}
.svc-split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 0.9fr;gap:clamp(2rem,4vw,4rem);align-items:start;}
.svc-split .svc-checklist,.svc-split .lead-p{max-width:none;}
.svc-split__media image-slot{width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:4/5;border-radius:var(--r-sm);}
@media(max-width:900px){.svc-split{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.svc-split__media{order:-1;max-width:440px;}}
.svc-split--rev{grid-template-columns:0.9fr 1.1fr;}
.svc-split--rev .svc-split__media{order:-1;}
@media(max-width:900px){.svc-split--rev{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}
.cs-nav{display:flex;gap:0.5rem;}
.cs-nav__btn{width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--cm-ink-800);border:1px solid var(--cm-border-strong);color:var(--cm-text-strong);font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1;cursor:pointer;transition:background var(--dur-2),color var(--dur-2);}
.cs-nav__btn:hover{background:var(--cm-accent);color:var(--cm-accent-contrast);border-color:var(--cm-accent);}
.cs-scroll{display:flex;gap:clamp(1.2rem,2.5vw,2rem);overflow-x:auto;scroll-snap-type:x mandatory;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;margin-top:1.8rem;padding-bottom:1rem;scrollbar-width:thin;}
.cs-card{flex:0 0 min(92%,560px);scroll-snap-align:start;}
.cs-card__media image-slot{width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:4/3;border-radius:var(--r-sm);}
.cs-card h3{margin-top:1.2rem;font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:var(--w-semibold);color:var(--cm-text-strong);letter-spacing:-0.01em;}
.cs-card .svc-checklist{margin-top:0.8rem;}
.svc-faq{max-width:68ch;}
.svc-faq .faq-list{border-top:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);margin-top:1.8rem;}
.svc-faq .faq-item{border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);}
.svc-faq .faq-item p a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;text-decoration-color:var(--cm-border-strong);transition:text-decoration-color var(--dur-2);}
.svc-faq .faq-item p a:hover{text-decoration-color:currentColor;}
.svc-faq .faq-item summary{list-style:none;cursor:pointer;padding:1.3rem 0;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:2rem;align-items:center;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:var(--w-semibold);font-size:1rem;color:var(--cm-text-strong);}
.svc-faq .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none;}
.svc-faq .faq-item .pm{position:relative;width:16px;height:16px;flex:none;}
.svc-faq .faq-item .pm::before,.svc-faq .faq-item .pm::after{content:"";position:absolute;background:var(--cm-silver);transition:transform var(--dur-3);}
.svc-faq .faq-item .pm::before{top:7.5px;left:0;width:16px;height:1.5px;}
.svc-faq .faq-item .pm::after{top:0;left:7.5px;width:1.5px;height:16px;}
.svc-faq .faq-item[open] .pm::after{transform:scaleY(0);}
.svc-faq .faq-item p{margin-top:0;padding:0 0 1.3rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);}
</style>
</Fragment>

<main>
<div class="container breadcrumb"><a href="/architectural-scale-models">← Architectural scale models</a></div>

<section class="page-hero"><div class="container">
  <div class="page-hero__inner">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Services / Architecture &amp; Real Estate</span>
      <h1 class="display-lg measure">Trade Show &amp;<br><em>Convention</em><br>Models</h1>
      <p class="lead measure">Bring your project to the next venue.</p>
      <p class="muted measure" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">Carve Model creates architectural presentation models for trade shows and conventions. We plan the model around what you need to communicate, the space available in your booth and how it will travel between events.</p>
      <div class="hero__cta">
        <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact">Get a Preliminary Estimate <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/works">View Our Work <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="page-hero__visual reveal">
      <span class="corner tl"></span><span class="corner br"></span>
      <image-slot id="tsc-hero" placeholder="Drop trade show model photo" src="/assets/trade-show-aviation-garage.webp"></image-slot>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Clear communication</span>
  <h2>Make the project easy to understand</h2>
  <div class="svc-split svc-split--rev" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">
    <div>
      <p class="lead-p muted" style="margin-top:0;">A trade-show model gives visitors a physical reference for conversations with your team. It can show the overall development, explain relationships between buildings and highlight the features that matter to your audience.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">We help define what should be included, emphasized or simplified so the model remains clear at its intended viewing distance.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">Depending on the project, the model can present:</p>
      <ul class="svc-checklist">
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Building forms and architectural features.</li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Site layout, access and surrounding context.</li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Landscaping, amenities and shared spaces.</li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Interior arrangements through sections or removable elements.</li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Selected areas highlighted by lighting.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="svc-split__media"><image-slot id="tsc-clear" placeholder="Drop a project photo" src="/assets/type-presentation.webp"></image-slot></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Portability</span>
  <h2>Plan portability from the beginning</h2>
  <div class="svc-split" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">
    <div>
      <p class="lead-p muted" style="margin-top:0;">A model that travels to several venues needs to be designed around transportation and handling.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">Before setting its dimensions, we review:</p>
      <ul class="svc-checklist">
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Whether it will be carried, transported by vehicle or shipped.</li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> How many people will handle it.</li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Booth dimensions and display-table requirements.</li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Case dimensions, storage and access restrictions.</li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Available setup time and electrical connections.</li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> The number and frequency of planned events.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="svc-note">Where appropriate, the model can be divided into sections or fitted with removable components. We balance portability with the detail needed for an effective presentation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="svc-split__media"><image-slot id="tsc-portable" placeholder="Drop a project photo" src="/assets/svc-arch-features.webp"></image-slot></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Protection</span>
  <h2>Protect the model between events</h2>
  <div class="svc-split svc-split--rev" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">
    <div>
      <p class="lead-p muted" style="margin-top:0;">Protective packaging is planned alongside the model. Depending on its size and construction, this may include a fitted transport case, protective crating or separately packed components.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">We consider vulnerable details, handling points and how components will be secured during travel. Repeated-use requirements also inform the choice of materials and finishes.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">The quotation specifies the packaging and transport provisions included in the scope.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="svc-split__media"><image-slot id="tsc-protect" placeholder="Drop a project photo" src="/assets/casestudy-atlanta3-1200.webp"></image-slot></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Setup</span>
  <h2>Keep setup practical</h2>
  <div class="svc-split" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">
    <div>
      <p class="lead-p muted" style="margin-top:0;">We review how the model will be unpacked, assembled, positioned and connected at each venue.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">For models with lighting or separate sections, connections and assembly requirements are considered during design. Tell us whether your own team will handle setup or whether you need installation support.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="svc-split__media"><image-slot id="tsc-setup" placeholder="Drop a project photo" src="/assets/svc-arch-support.webp"></image-slot></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Digital presentation</span>
  <h2>Add digital presentation where useful</h2>
  <div class="svc-split svc-split--rev" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">
    <div>
      <p class="lead-p muted" style="margin-top:0;">A physical model can be presented alongside animation, touchscreen content, AR or VR to explain details that are difficult to show at model scale.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">Digital content can extend the presentation into interiors, viewpoints or design options while the model provides the overall project context. Content, hardware and integration requirements are scoped separately.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="svc-split__media"><image-slot id="tsc-digital" placeholder="Drop a project photo" src="/assets/svc-arch-defining.webp"></image-slot></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Budget and schedule</span>
  <h2>Budget and schedule</h2>
  <p class="lead-p muted">Pricing depends on the model’s size, detail, materials, features, packaging and delivery requirements. Travel-ready construction and repeated setup requirements are part of the scope.</p>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;max-width:68ch;">Share your first event date early so we can plan fabrication, approvals, packing and delivery around it. If several events are scheduled, include their locations and dates.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section" style="border-bottom:0;"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Start with what you have</span>
  <h2>Send us the information you have</h2>
  <div class="formats">
    <div class="fmt">Drawings, renderings or available 3D files</div>
    <div class="fmt">The project features you want visitors to understand</div>
    <div class="fmt">Booth space and preferred model dimensions</div>
    <div class="fmt">How the model will travel and who will handle it</div>
    <div class="fmt">Lighting or digital-presentation requirements</div>
    <div class="fmt">Event dates and delivery locations</div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="cta reveal" style="position:relative;text-align:center;background:var(--cm-black);border:1px solid var(--cm-border);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:clamp(3rem,6vw,5rem) var(--gutter);">
    <h2 class="display-md">Start your trade-show model.</h2>
    <p class="muted mt-2" style="max-width:52ch;margin-inline:auto;">We will review the information and recommend a scope that balances presentation quality with practical transport and setup.</p>
    <div class="hero__cta" style="justify-content:center;margin-top:2.4rem;">
      <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact">Get a Preliminary Estimate <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/architectural-scale-models">Architectural Model Services <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
